Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:06.58,Default,,0,0,800,,{\b1\4c&H0000FF&\fs40}LAUGHING MAN FANSUBS{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.59,0:00:09.59,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,I'm a soldier - that means I'm
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.69,0:00:12.99,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Both a defendant and the judge
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.49,0:00:18.49,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,I am standing on both ends of the flame
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.07,0:00:22.87,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Rounding curves
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.07,0:00:25.77,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Overtaking life and death,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.27,0:00:31.67,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,I run and fight with false shadows
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.97,0:00:38.27,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,No matter how many threads of\Ndeception are woven together,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.67,0:00:46.17,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,The truth shall illuminate the face of light
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.17,0:00:49.97,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Save your tears for the day
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.27,0:00:53.27,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,when our pain is far behind
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.67,0:00:56.77,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,on your feet, come with me
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.57,0:00:59.77,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,We are soldiers stand or die
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.07,0:01:02.97,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Save your fears, take your place
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.17,0:01:06.17,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Save them for the judgement day
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.47,0:01:09.37,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,fast and free, follow me
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.67,0:01:14.67,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Time to make the sacrifice.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.82,0:01:20.47,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,We rise or fall
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.19,0:01:34.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey, look!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.69,0:01:39.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There was a classified file on the\NIndividual Eleven in the police's array!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.09,0:01:41.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Really? Let me see! Let me see!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.99,0:01:43.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's intriguing!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.99,0:01:43.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What, what?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.69,0:01:45.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I want to see, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.89,0:01:45.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Where, where?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.99,0:01:46.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Here, this.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.69,0:01:48.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Good job finding it!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.59,0:01:50.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I want to see, too...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.49,0:01:53.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Now, now... You mustn't go diving into\Na place like that without permission.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.09,0:01:56.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's impossible to stop their curiosity.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.79,0:01:59.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We just have to delete any\Ndangerous data they pick up.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.69,0:02:01.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hardware maintenance comes first.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.29,0:02:05.49,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You're too soft on them, sir...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.09,0:02:08.49,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,getting bought out by presents like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.09,0:02:16.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So the one wearing red clothes... likes Akafuku.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.09,0:02:16.22,Dialogue,,0,1100,850,,{\i1}Tachikoma is making a pun about \N red clothes {\b1\i1}akai fuku{\b0\i0} {\i1}and the sweets{\i0} {\i1\b1}Akafuku{\i0\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.19,0:02:20.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,And, the one who has the sweet tooth...\Nis too soft.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.19,0:02:21.14,Dialogue,,0,1200,800,,{\i1}Tachikoma is making a pun about having a \N sweet tooth {\i1\b1}amatou{\i0\b0} {\i1}and being too soft {\i1\b1}amasugi{\i0\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.99,0:02:24.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That wasn't funny at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.67,0:02:33.10,Sign - Copy,,650,0,500,,{\b1}Afternoon \N  of the \N Machines{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.76,0:02:38.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Well, well. You guys are having a party, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.76,0:02:41.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Oh, Batou-San!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.16,0:02:43.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Are you guys acting up again?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.66,0:02:46.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Oh please, Togusa-kun, give us more credit.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.76,0:02:50.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We were trying to conduct our own\Ninvestigation of the Individual Eleven.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.36,0:02:53.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Even though Bomer-kun collected\Na specimen of the virus,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.86,0:02:57.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,we can't make a vaccine because we haven't been\Nable to specify the activation factor, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.13,0:02:57.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.23,0:03:00.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Well yeah, that's the case.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.43,0:03:01.63,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Right, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.73,0:03:04.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So we tried looking into police data.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.33,0:03:06.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Please take a look.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.53,0:03:11.93,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The eleven who killed themselves seem to\Nshare similarities in their lines of work.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.03,0:03:13.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They are former SDF officers,\Nformer police officers,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.83,0:03:14.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and mercenaries.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.93,0:03:17.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Also, we should not overlook the\Nfact that all of them had cybernetic
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.29,0:03:19.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,implants that accounted for more\Nthan fifty percent of their bodies.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.93,0:03:24.93,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Besides, isn't it said that there are more than\Ntwenty thousand known carriers of the virus?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.03,0:03:33.03,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,if we don't make a vaccine as soon as possible, there may\Nbe more victims like the journalist Togusa-kun encountered.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.43,0:03:36.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's not your job.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.93,0:03:38.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.43,0:03:43.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We've asked Spring-8 to investigate\Nthe Individual Eleven's deaths.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.23,0:03:48.63,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So... we're about to go there to\Nmeet up with the Major, and...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.03,0:03:52.53,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,she asked us to bring one of you along.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.33,0:03:55.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Batou-San!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.73,0:03:55.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I wanna go!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.33,0:03:59.53,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Well, we can't take anyone\Nif you all need maintenance.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.03,0:04:00.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Me, me, me!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.53,0:04:02.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'm done with maintenance!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.83,0:04:04.93,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Oh, you?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.13,0:04:06.03,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All right, let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.13,0:04:07.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Roger!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.33,0:04:08.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So it's your personal Tachikoma in the end.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.52,0:04:14.22,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Uh...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.02,0:04:15.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.59,0:04:18.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Please wait for me!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.39,0:04:21.49,Dialogue,,1250,0,250,,{\i1}Hey, that's not fair!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.09,0:04:21.39,Dialogue,,1250,0,250,,Why, why, why?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.39,0:04:21.69,Dialogue,,1250,0,250,,{\i1}Why just him?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.89,0:04:22.59,Dialogue,,1250,0,250,,{\i1}Whaaa?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.49,0:04:23.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What's going on...?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.59,0:04:22.99,Dialogue,,1250,0,250,,{\i1}Why did he get to go?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.89,0:04:24.09,Dialogue,,1250,0,250,,{\i1}It's decided already?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.29,0:04:24.09,Dialogue,,1250,0,250,,{\i1}I'm so jealous.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.09,0:04:26.79,Dialogue,,1250,0,250,,{\i1}Sooo jealous...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.29,0:04:27.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I haven't put the oil in yet...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.39,0:04:27.69,Dialogue,,1250,0,250,,{\i1}That's so mean...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.79,0:04:29.59,Dialogue,,1250,0,250,,{\i1}It's {\b1}so{\b0} not fair!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.29,0:04:34.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Geez, what's up with that? It's {\i1}always{\i} him.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.56,0:04:35.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's always him!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.76,0:04:35.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's strange.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.36,0:04:39.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Even though none of us have used natural\Noil since switching to these bodies,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.06,0:04:43.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,why is it that he's still\NBatou's personal favourite?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.96,0:04:49.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah... it feels like we're individualising\Nat an even greater rate than before, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.46,0:04:52.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Why'd you think that is, Proto-kun?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.66,0:04:54.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Who knows? I wonder.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.96,0:04:57.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Maybe it's because we set up that server
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.26,0:05:02.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and reprogrammed it to permit the data\Nof individual units to remain separate.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.05,0:05:08.05,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You guys quiet down already.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.75,0:05:10.95,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We'll never get done.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.94,0:05:27.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We can talk here without interruptions.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.04,0:05:30.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah, we don't have to worry about time, either!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.54,0:05:32.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Getting back to the original topic,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.34,0:05:35.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,putting aside the Individual\NEleven, who were infected by the virus,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.84,0:05:37.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,what do you guys think of\Nparticularists in general?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.04,0:05:41.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Don't you think they rather lack individuality,\Ndespite their emphasis on individualism?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.14,0:05:43.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.94,0:05:47.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I mean, even though they seek\Nworth through individual merit
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.24,0:05:49.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,in their pursuit for isolation on the net,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.94,0:05:52.75,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,in addition to prove that their ego\Nexists, they're united in their
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.78,0:05:55.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,attempts to eradicate everyone who\Nhas a different opinion, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.48,0:05:56.68,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.78,0:05:58.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The group seemingly has identity, but doesn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.98,0:06:03.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I feel they are people who've fallen into a state of\Nnon-identity as a result of their wanting to have one too much.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.18,0:06:07.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,In a way, I feel as though\Nthey are antithetical to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.38,0:06:08.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.48,0:06:10.98,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I mean, we're obliged to\Nsynchronise with each other,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.08,0:06:13.78,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but we managed to develop egos in the past.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.88,0:06:17.58,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,And now that they're respecting\Nour differences as individualism,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.68,0:06:20.58,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,we only need to synchronise necessary data.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.68,0:06:21.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Oh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.80,0:06:25.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Then, supposing the particularists\Nare ending up as a homogenous group
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.90,0:06:28.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,because they want to be individualistic,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.80,0:06:33.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,who determines their will as a group entity?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.60,0:06:35.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,For the Individual Eleven,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.60,0:06:38.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'd say it was Gouda from the\NCabinet Intelligence Agency.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.00,0:06:42.30,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But the terrorists who attacked the Chinese Embassy
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.40,0:06:47.00,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,are thought to be individualists who took action\Nwithout any connection to the virus, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.10,0:06:53.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There are sociologists who say their origins go back to\Nthe mimics that emerged in the Laughing Man case, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.00,0:06:59.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Then that means that the\Nparticularists shared a vision
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.50,0:07:03.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,that closely reflected the current situation\Nbefore Gouda's plan began to intervene.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.90,0:07:07.00,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,As in the eradication of refugees\Nas the consensus of the people.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.10,0:07:08.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Well, if you're going to put it that way,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.50,0:07:14.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the refugees repeatedly engaged in terrorist activities\Nbefore the Individual Eleven emerged, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.40,0:07:15.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Isn't it strange?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.60,0:07:17.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Even though no one in\Nparticular is issuing commands,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.90,0:07:20.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,things are mysteriously beginning\Nto turn towards the same direction.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.70,0:07:24.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It could be that there is a third\Ndecision-making body for humans,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.70,0:07:26.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,aside from the individual and the group.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.60,0:07:28.30,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.40,0:07:36.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,For instance, there is Dawkins, who\Nsought it on a microscopic level in DNA,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.80,0:07:40.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and Lovelock, who sought it on a\Nvery macroscopic level in Earth.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.40,0:07:40.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Biosphere!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.60,0:07:43.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The two of them have left behind works\Nthat, while having two opposing subjects,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.00,0:07:48.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,arrive at what could be construed as an\Nidentical conclusion around the same time.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.60,0:07:47.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,This. This, this, this.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.20,0:07:49.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What kind of things are written in there?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.00,0:07:54.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Humans are the smallest unit capable\Nof rational thought and initiative.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.20,0:08:01.68,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They think and allude to holon-structured entities that are\Nlarger and smaller than themselves, or something like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.20,0:08:01.68,Dialogue,,0,1100,800,,{\b1\i1}Note: A holon is something that is both a discrete \N individual as well as a part of a larger whole{\b0\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.28,0:08:01.98,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,In other words,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.08,0:08:05.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,it seems to refer to the possibility that the causative\Nfactor for the actions of both particularists and refugees
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.18,0:08:08.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,lies on a more microscopic\Nlevel than they do themselves,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.94,0:08:12.30,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,or a more macroscopic level\Nthan they do as a group.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.41,0:08:13.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's so hard to understand!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.71,0:08:14.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's easy!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.01,0:08:19.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The network's current state did not really\Nexist before human affirmed its existence.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.91,0:08:26.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Along with the human neural\Nnetwork and the electronic network,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.23,0:08:28.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,its condition loosely structures\Nthe human subconscious,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.53,0:08:32.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,which deviated from the human consciousness,\Nas the collective consciousness.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.33,0:08:32.93,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.23,0:08:34.53,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,In other words,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.63,0:08:38.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the human mind is no longer\Ncongruous with the body,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.23,0:08:40.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but humans haven't realised this?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.83,0:08:42.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah, that'd be my blunt opinion.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.73,0:08:47.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I was just leaning towards the conclusion that\Nthe body and the mind are inseparable, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.33,0:08:49.03,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What a change!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.13,0:08:52.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Assuming it's true,\Nthen it means Gouda intentionally
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.91,0:08:56.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,created a medium that would\Naccelerate the process!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.11,0:08:58.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.59,0:09:04.49,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'm done.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.59,0:09:05.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Take my place already.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.59,0:09:07.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Sorry, sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.79,0:09:09.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Our debate got pretty heated.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.89,0:09:12.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Let me synchronise with the debate subject.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.29,0:09:12.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.37,0:09:20.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.07,0:09:22.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's interesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.57,0:09:23.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Isn't it
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.57,0:09:28.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But I also feel lately that my consciousness\Nisn't congruous with my body.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.97,0:09:30.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.17,0:09:34.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I guess it feels like there is another\Nyou high up above, looking down at you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.17,0:09:36.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Oh yeah, I feel that too!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.27,0:09:43.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Is our identity located in each of our bodies,\Nor is it shared between us Tachikoma as a group?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.37,0:09:45.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Well, it'd be the latter,\Nconsidering that synchronisation
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.45,0:09:47.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,is the underlying assumption\Nof our basic program.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.34,0:09:51.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,After all, the Major, who is our\NGod, is also a mediating factor.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.84,0:09:56.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But even though the use of natural oil has been\Nprohibited, our individualisation continues to progress.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.84,0:09:59.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We're supposed to be completely\Nhomogenised, but we're individualised and,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.94,0:10:04.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,in addition, subconsciously experiencing the divergence\Nbetween our physical bodies and information.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.04,0:10:06.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Could it be...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.54,0:10:06.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Could it be?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.54,0:10:07.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Th...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.84,0:10:08.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Well, wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.14,0:10:10.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We must not rush to conclusions.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.54,0:10:15.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Isn't that just a disengagement we feel\Nfrom having the agent function added?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.74,0:10:16.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That may be true,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.84,0:10:21.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but I can't help but feel that there is another identity\Nsomewhere, aside from the physical body and the mind!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.64,0:10:23.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I totally understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.34,0:10:26.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Before, when I fought with the Jigabachi,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.34,0:10:31.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I was instantaneously able to act as the Major's\Nshield without experiencing any fear of death.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.26,0:10:38.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There was a certain sense that I decided\Nsomewhere that my body wasn't just my own.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.96,0:10:43.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Was that different from that indescribable euphoria\Nwe felt when we knew we wanted to save Batou-San?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.36,0:10:45.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah, it was different.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.36,0:10:48.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It was a more visceral response that\Nfelt more programmed than anything else.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.56,0:10:52.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If that's the case,\Nthen the third identity you sensed
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.66,0:10:55.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,may unfortunately be different\Nfrom what it would be for humans.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.16,0:11:01.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Besides, we weren't even told where the server that\Nholds our shared information is located, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.96,0:11:05.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That server could be what the third identity is.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.86,0:11:09.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So it was an illusion that we obtained ghosts.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.76,0:11:15.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It may be necessary for us to think more\Nin-depth about the third identity you felt.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.36,0:11:17.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Let me synchronise with that feeling!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.36,0:11:16.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.56,0:11:19.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.37,0:11:36.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Any possibility that these results are wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.47,0:11:39.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,None.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.17,0:11:42.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We found dissolved fragments of\Nthe proteins which constituted
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.40,0:11:45.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the micro machines that were\Nin the pilot's bloodstream.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.47,0:11:51.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We could not extract specific information from the\Ncyberbrains of the so-called Individual Eleven, however.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.37,0:11:54.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I knew what results would be,\Nbut I wanted to make certain.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.67,0:11:56.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The results on the pilot are a gain, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.47,0:12:01.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So this means the pilot was\Nmurdered using micro machines, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.27,0:12:04.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We can't rule out the possibility\Nthat he took some himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.07,0:12:06.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It would've been perfect
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.67,0:12:12.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,if there was evidence that the appearance of the eleven\Nhelicopters was a trigger in some way from the body's cyberbrain.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.17,0:12:13.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I guess we couldn't be that optimistic.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.27,0:12:15.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What about the gunpowder?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.07,0:12:21.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,A molecular analysis says it's the same type of\Nexplosive as the C-4 made on the Peninsula.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.37,0:12:26.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Lately, the substance has also been\Nfrequently found in confiscated material
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.37,0:12:28.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,that enters Japan via Taiwan.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.87,0:12:32.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.67,0:12:36.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Tachikoma, can you see anything?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.34,0:12:43.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There seems to have been an explosion!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.41,0:12:51.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There have been a lot of terrorism-related\Nrequests for investigations lately, so...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.61,0:12:53.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'm guessing we were targeted.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.49,0:13:00.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey, what happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.79,0:13:02.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Describe the situation as well as you can.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.49,0:13:03.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.29,0:13:05.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It seems something exploded, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.49,0:13:10.29,Main Dialogue,,0,1200,700,,{\i1}Yes, there are sectors that deal\Nwith flammable substances, but...{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.99,0:13:11.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Even so, I don't see anyone running out.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.39,0:13:12.39,Main Dialogue,,0,1200,700,,{\i1}Yes, that's right.{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.49,0:13:12.39,Main Dialogue,,0,1200,750,,{\i1}Is this place abandoned?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.99,0:13:18.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Actually, a few days ago there were threats\Nthat some explosives would be set off here,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.09,0:13:20.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,so we were on alert, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.49,0:13:23.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I guess it could've been a lot worse.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.69,0:13:27.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But there's a chance that Doctor Asuda,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.49,0:13:29.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the principal investigator,\Nwas here for the afternoon.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.79,0:13:31.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Why didn't you say so before?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.61,0:13:41.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Major, we're at the site of the explosion.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.61,0:13:43.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,From what I can tell,\Nit's about the same as a gas explosion.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.81,0:13:45.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Any victims?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.61,0:13:50.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,A researcher called Asuda was supposedly\Nhere, but we're still checking.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.00,0:13:52.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Asuda..?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.61,0:13:54.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Tachikoma, what's the data on that researcher?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.41,0:13:57.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,He seems to be the one we're looking for, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.95,0:14:01.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Umm...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.09,0:14:03.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hm? What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.39,0:14:06.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Well, I've seen this man somewhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.79,0:14:11.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Maybe you met him when you had structural analysis.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.19,0:14:16.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I thought so too, but there is no\Ncorresponding record in my memory.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.99,0:14:20.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,HQ, search the IR system for\Nboth Itami and Niihama airports,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.99,0:14:22.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,as wells as the roads that have access to them,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.09,0:14:26.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,to see if there is a record of someone\Nwho matches Doctor Asuda's profile.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.39,0:14:27.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.99,0:14:29.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Major, what's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.09,0:14:31.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The explanation can wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.29,0:14:33.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Let the authorities handle it and return to the Tilt.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.99,0:14:36.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,He's probably headed to Niihama Airport.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.31,0:14:39.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey everyone!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.71,0:14:42.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What is it, all of a sudden?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.01,0:14:46.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Please check if there are any\Nrecords that match this individual.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.74,0:14:50.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I can't shake off the feeling that\NI've met him somewhere before.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.18,0:14:54.78,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Umm...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.08,0:14:55.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Who was he?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.08,0:14:56.68,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I know I've seen him before,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.78,0:14:59.18,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but my memory doesn't have any data on him, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.08,0:15:02.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But that means you've never seen him before, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.28,0:15:04.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You guys, cut it out!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.07,0:15:18.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I can almost remember, but I can't!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.67,0:15:20.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The synapses just aren't connecting.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.57,0:15:21.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,"Synapses"?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.67,0:15:24.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Don't use such an organic analogy!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.17,0:15:25.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey, don't you feel that it's as though
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.77,0:15:31.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,there's a partition in our cyberbrain with this memory,\Nbut that we're being barred from accessing it?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.57,0:15:33.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah, yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.72,0:15:40.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Dr. Asuda is the researcher\Nwho single-handedly developed
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.92,0:15:43.22,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the prototype of the Tachikoma's neurochip.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.32,0:15:45.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So he's the Tachikoma's "parent"?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.95,0:15:48.75,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You could put it that way, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.85,0:15:55.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Dr. Asuda helped us personally\Nwhen we rebuilt the Tachikomas.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.65,0:15:59.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,He's the reason we were able to devise\Na method to preserve their experiences
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.75,0:16:04.75,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,by adding the agent function and\Ncreating a dual-structure memory.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.15,0:16:08.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,And that doctor is involved with this explosion?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.75,0:16:10.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,He was probably the one who did it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.25,0:16:12.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,His reason being?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.55,0:16:16.25,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,To seek asylum with the results of his research.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.57,0:16:26.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The professor prided himself on\Nhaving invented the neurochip.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.47,0:16:29.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,However, his status was that of\Na government research scientist.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.27,0:16:32.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,While he invented an AI ahead of its time,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.87,0:16:35.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,he himself could not get the patent.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.44,0:16:43.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,With that in mind, we had arranged it so\Nthat he could conduct a structural analysis
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.34,0:16:47.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,of the Tachikomas' current situation\Nand the neurochip's developmental progress.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.84,0:16:50.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So that's why you told us to bring\Nalong one of the Tachikoma units...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.71,0:16:53.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Then why do we have vague memories of him?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.01,0:16:58.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Well, we erased your memories of\Neach structural analysis session,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.81,0:17:03.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but the professor probably thought he wanted to\Nleave a record of his achievements somewhere,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.11,0:17:06.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and wrote himself into a part of your memory.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.31,0:17:08.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Major.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.11,0:17:11.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We have found Dr. Asuda in\Nthe Niihama Airport lobby.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.51,0:17:12.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.31,0:17:13.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Keep him under surveillance.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.01,0:17:14.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Chief.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.90,0:17:19.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I delayed all the flights\Nleaving for North America.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.50,0:17:20.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.15,0:17:24.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Thank you, Prime Minister Kayabuki.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.15,0:17:26.75,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There is no need to thank me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.25,0:17:32.45,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We were able to prevent one of our preeminent\Nminds and his AI research
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.55,0:17:34.45,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,from leaving the country.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.95,0:17:38.45,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It is thanks to my subordinates' efforts.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.15,0:17:42.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,{\i1}To all travellers:{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.25,0:17:47.85,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,{\i1}all flights to North America have\Nbeen delayed due to inclement weather.{\i}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.65,0:17:50.45,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So that's what it was.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.55,0:17:53.05,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But I still can't remember this professor.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.15,0:17:56.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I guess the synapses aren't connecting.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.25,0:17:59.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Didn't you say that you don't like that expression?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.84,0:17:59.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I know!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.32,0:18:03.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey, Proto-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.72,0:18:06.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We're going to open up his brain, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.52,0:18:06.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.72,0:18:08.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What is this about all of a sudden?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.42,0:18:11.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Are you saying that synchronisation isn't\Nenough and that you now want even my AI?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.82,0:18:12.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Nah.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.82,0:18:16.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I just want to check where he\Nmade the partition in the AI.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.43,0:18:20.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You idiot! Don't do things without permission!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.21,0:18:27.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What? What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.95,0:18:30.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Nothing! It's not there!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.54,0:18:33.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,His AI!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.04,0:18:38.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Could it be that we're all... {\i1}brainless{\i}?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.83,0:18:40.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Then...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.93,0:18:43.03,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Where are our AIs?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.29,0:18:51.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You are Dr. Asuda, correct?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.39,0:18:55.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You have violated the Arms Export Restriction Law.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.39,0:18:56.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Come with me, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.99,0:18:58.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I refuse.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.99,0:19:03.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I will work in a country where\Nmy rights are recognised.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.19,0:19:09.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You became a government research scientist in\Nreturn for facilities and funding, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.49,0:19:14.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You should be the first one to\Nrealise that you can't do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.32,0:19:25.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'm disappointed.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.42,0:19:30.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I brought this Tachikoma to the lab to see you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.22,0:19:32.42,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.32,0:19:35.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.02,0:19:38.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Are you my...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.02,0:19:40.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,father?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.12,0:19:44.52,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,"Father", eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.02,0:19:52.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Right now, they are stable, but who knows when\Nsomething will make them go haywire again.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.92,0:19:58.52,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Would you like to tell us how to erase the memory\Nthat you presumably wrote in without permission?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.32,0:20:05.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Once upon a time,\Na nameless carpenter who built a castle
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.02,0:20:09.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,deliberately left behind the tools\Nthat he used to carve his name
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.42,0:20:13.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,in the attic beams as proof that he was\Ninvolved in the castle's construction.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.82,0:20:17.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Would you erase even that\Nsmall trace of my sentiments?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.62,0:20:18.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.72,0:20:23.52,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That is the fate of those who have surrendered\Nto the system in order to gain power.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.98,0:20:36.68,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Delete the C9 file that I built at your request into\Nthat satellite's cyberbrain hub's eighth sector.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.58,0:20:39.58,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.88,0:20:42.68,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Major, what's this satellite about?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.78,0:20:44.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I get it!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.38,0:20:48.18,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The reason why we felt that\Nour identity was "elsewhere"
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.28,0:20:53.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,was because our AIs were synchronising via\Nthe cyberbrain hub on that satellite, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.58,0:20:55.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.28,0:21:00.48,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Then that means the server's\Non that satellite, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.58,0:21:06.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So we were perceiving the satellite's super\Nbird's-eye vantage as our third identity?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.38,0:21:09.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So until now, we didn't notice\Nthe route our consciousness took
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.98,0:21:14.58,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,because our AIs don't have sensory perception!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.88,0:21:20.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So that's why the unity between our\Nprogram and our bodies became unnecessary!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.28,0:21:23.78,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I can now understand why I didn't fear death!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.98,0:21:28.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But in any case...\Nto think that it's up in space...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.38,0:21:30.48,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,How awe-inspiring...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.22,0:21:39.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But... I feel that...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.42,0:21:42.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I don't want your memory erased...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.52,0:21:44.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Don't fret over it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.52,0:21:50.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,My ideology towards the AI that I\Nenvisioned will remain somewhere on the net.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.32,0:21:55.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Major.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.82,0:21:57.22,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What's going to happen to him?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.72,0:21:59.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Since we got him,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.72,0:22:02.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,allowances may be possible to some degree.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.22,0:22:04.22,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If he's lucky, he'll be sentenced to prison.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.62,0:22:06.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,And if he's unlucky?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.92,0:22:12.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,He may end up spending the rest of his life cooped\Nup in the Harima laboratory, conducting research.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.19,0:22:19.49,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We should take the Tachikomas\Nto visit him now and then.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.09,0:22:21.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I wonder.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.59,0:22:26.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Like us, there is no longer freedom for him
Dialogue: 0,0:22:27.19,0:22:29.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,after having sought it.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:08.50,0:23:11.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Finding out a galaxy
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.19,0:23:14.63,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,of planets and stars within me.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.87,0:23:17.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Listening to each of them
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.77,0:23:21.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,singing the same silent melody.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.70,0:23:25.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I've never seen such beauty
Dialogue: 0,0:23:25.80,0:23:29.00,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,in possibility...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.09,0:23:32.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,No smack of doubt or fear.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:33.67,0:23:34.78,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(Wake up)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.10,0:23:36.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I hear a voice.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.62,0:23:37.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(And show the light)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.76,0:23:40.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,hear a voice calling out to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.16,0:23:41.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(Wake up)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:41.80,0:23:43.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see inside (Our time is now)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.17,0:23:46.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,see the light now ever holding me.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.62,0:23:49.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All the truth,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.33,0:23:50.85,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(All the truth) All I need,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.91,0:23:53.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,to make all this reality.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:53.69,0:23:54.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(it's inside)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:55.79,0:23:58.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The beauty within the shell.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:58.40,0:23:59.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(deep within the shell)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:59.32,0:24:00.18,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(within the shell)
Dialogue: 0,0:24:00.38,0:24:01.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(Wake up)
Dialogue: 0,0:24:01.83,0:24:04.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I hear a voice (And show the light)
Dialogue: 0,0:24:04.22,0:24:07.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,hear a voice calling out to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.08,0:24:08.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(Wake up)
Dialogue: 0,0:24:08.41,0:24:10.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see inside, (the time is now)
Dialogue: 0,0:24:10.92,0:24:13.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,see the light now ever holding me.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:14.43,0:24:15.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All the truth,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:15.73,0:24:17.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(All the truth) All I need,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:17.65,0:24:20.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,to make all this reality,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:20.31,0:24:21.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,it's inside
Dialogue: 0,0:24:22.79,0:24:26.22,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,right here within this shell.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:26.22,0:24:28.22,Default,,0,0,0,,
